**Blocked — Test how robust the emulated profile shapes and the HSE mass are to feedback (AGN and SN) parameters and to halo mass, at the same two redshifts, and check whether the emulated profiles depart from self-similarity..** (The tool budget ran out after the predictions were made but before the variant CSVs could be read and compared, so slopes, M_HSE changes, plots and the self-similarity test were not done. The halo-mass test cannot be done with this emulator because mass is not an input.) Not finished: none of the d-02 success criteria are met yet. The predictions exist but only the fiducial z=0 profiles have been analysed.

What the emulator offers (f-007):
- CGD comes out as rho_gas/rho_crit and CTP as T/T500. Both are on 19 log-spaced bins of r/R500 from 0.015 to 2.74.
- Halo mass is not an input, so group-versus-cluster mass bins cannot be tested with this tool (dead end x-01).
- The profiles exist only for z = 0 to 0.4987, so z = 0.4987 is the high-redshift point.
- The tool describes all five subgrid parameters as AGN parameters: kappa_w and e_w (wind) and M_seed, v_kin and eps_kin (kinetic). It lists no separate SN feedback parameter, so the wind extremes were used as a stand-in for the SN test. This needs checking against the HACC emulator paper.

Fiducial run (f-008): z=0 with kappa_w=3, e_w=0.6, M_seed=1.3, v_kin=0.65, eps_kin=0.61, omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8.
- At R500, finite differences between the 0.866 and 1.155 bins give dln rho_gas/dln r = -2.55 +/- 0.16 and dln T/dln r = -0.58 +/- 0.06.
- At 0.5 R500 the slopes are about -1.98 and -0.31. T/T500 at R500 is 0.59.
- M_HSE(R500) = 1.85 +/- 0.3 in units of k_B T500 R500/(G mu m_p). This equals 0.93 M500 only if the emulator defines T500 = G mu m_p M500/(2 R500), which is unconfirmed.
- I computed these by hand from the CSV. The errors treat neighbouring bins as independent and are probably too large.

Predictions not yet read (f-009): CGD and CTP at z=0 and z=0.4987 for five parameter sets:
- fiducial (d02_fid; the z=0 fiducial files are in the top-level run directory)
