[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "Redshift shift compared with kinetic-AGN spread. Approximation: dln n/dln r is held at the fiducial d-01 value (-2.54 at z=0, -2.74 at z=0.4987) for 
[finding] f-011 Redshift shift compared with kinetic-AGN spread. Approximation: dln n/dln r is held at the fiducial d-01 value (-2.54 at z=0, -2.74 at z=0.4987) for both varian
**Finding:** Redshift shift compared with kinetic-AGN spread. Approximation: dln n/dln r is held at the fiducial d-01 value (-2.54 at z=0, -2.74 at z=0.4987) for both variants, and M_HSE ∝ t(s_n+s_T). On that basis, the z=0 to 0.4987 change in ln t(R500) is -0.144 for AGN-min and -0.132 for AGN-max. The fiducial value from d-01 is -0.134. This is about twice the AGN spread in ln t at fixed z (0.060 at z=0, 0.071 at z=0.4987), so the redshift drop in scaled temperature is robust to kinetic-AGN feedback. For M_HSE,500c the picture is different. The shape-only redshift shift is -9.0% (AGN-min) or -5.6% (AGN-max) in ln M, against the fiducial -9.2%. The AGN-max minus AGN-min difference at fixed z is +4.6% at z=0 and +8.1% at z=0.4987. These are of the same size, so the M_HSE redshift shift cannot be cleanly separated from kinetic-feedback uncertainty. The GP y_std on t(R500) is about 1% at z=0 and 2-3% at z=0.4987, so the AGN spread in t is about 4 sigma at z=0 and about 2 sigma at z=0.4987.
