[direction] d-06 -> closed
**Completed — Limited feedback-robustness check. Using the existing d02_agnmin and d02_agnmax CTP predictions, measure how much t(R500) and the temperature slope move across the kinetic-AGN extremes. Compare that spread with the z=0 to z=0.4987 shift in the fiducial profiles..** I read the four kinetic-AGN CTP files with read_text_file (tc-...-90 to -93). Their paths are runs/261020_110147/d02_agnmin/CTP_z{0.0000,0.4987}_prediction.csv and runs/261020_110147/d02_agnmax/CTP_z{0.0000,0.4987}_prediction.csv. load_table_data could not be used because it fails on the CSV header row (dead end x-02). All derived numbers below are hand calculations from the tool-returned bin values. t(R500) is the geometric mean of the 0.866 and 1.155 R500 bins, and the slope is ln(t2/t1)/0.2877.

Results (f-010), as t(R500) and dlnT/dlnr:
- AGN-min (v_kin=0.1, eps_kin=0.02): 0.565 and -0.617 at z=0; 0.490 and -0.589 at z=0.4987.
- AGN-max (v_kin=1.2, eps_kin=1.2): 0.600 and -0.573 at z=0; 0.526 and -0.621 at z=0.4987.
- The AGN spread in t(R500) is 6.0% at z=0 and 7.1% at z=0.4987.
- The slope spread is only 0.03-0.04, and its sign reverses between the two redshifts.

Comparison (f-011):
- Temperature: the z=0 to 0.4987 change in ln t(R500) is -0.144 (AGN-min) and -0.132 (AGN-max), against -0.134 fiducial. This is about twice the AGN spread in ln t at fixed z, so the redshift cooling in scaled temperature is robust to kinetic-AGN feedback. The GP y_std on t(R500) is about 1% at z=0 and 2-3% at z=0.4987.
- Hydrostatic mass: I held the density slope at the fiducial d-01 values (-2.54 at z=0, -2.74 at z=0.4987; f-004, contested). On that basis the shape-only shift in ln M_HSE,500c is -9.0% (AGN-min) and -5.6% (AGN-max). The AGN-max minus AGN-min difference at fixed z is +4.6% at z=0 and +8.1% at z=0.4987. The M_HSE redshift shift is therefore about the same size as the kinetic-AGN spread and cannot be cleanly separated from it to first order.

Not done: the wind variants (d02_windmin, d02_windmax), the variant CGD density profiles and density slopes (the full density analysis), the M_seed variation, and comparison plots.
