[tool] d-04 post_finding {"claim": "Nelson+14 f_nth correction at R500, using A=0.452, B=0.841, gamma=1.628 and P_tot = P_th/(1-f). The formula is M_tot/M500 = (t/2)/(1-f) * [-(s_n+s_T)
[finding] f-013 Nelson+14 f_nth correction at R500, using A=0.452, B=0.841, gamma=1.628 and P_tot = P_th/(1-f). The formula is M_tot/M500 = (t/2)/(1-f) * [-(s_n+s_T) + dln(1-f)
**Finding (preliminary):** Nelson+14 f_nth correction at R500, using A=0.452, B=0.841, gamma=1.628 and P_tot = P_th/(1-f). The formula is M_tot/M500 = (t/2)/(1-f) * [-(s_n+s_T) + dln(1-f)/dln r], with dln(1-f)/dln r = -gamma*u*e^-u/(1+e^-u) and u = (r/R200m/B)^gamma. For the radius conversion I assumed an NFW profile with c200c=4 and Omega_m=0.3, which gives R500c = 0.652 R200c. R200m is 1.69 R200c at z=0 (Omega_m(z)=0.30) and 1.265 R200c at z=0.4987 (Omega_m(z)=0.59), so R200m/R500c = 2.60 and 1.94. At z=0: R500 = 0.385 R200m, f_nth = 0.207 and dln(1-f)/dln r = -0.196, so M_tot/M500 = 0.3728 * 2.932 = 1.093. At z=0.4987: R500 = 0.515 R200m, f_nth = 0.260 and dln(1-f)/dln r = -0.285, so M_tot/M500 = 0.3500 * 2.958 = 1.035. The corrected b_HSE is +0.09 (z=0) and +0.035 (z=0.4987), which overcorrects. The correction factor M_tot/M_th is 1.18 at z=0 and 1.23 at z=0.4987, and the corrected redshift shift is -5.3% instead of -9.2%. If R200m/R500c is held at 2.60 at both redshifts, the shift stays at -9.2%. So the redshift dependence of the correction comes entirely from the assumed evolution of R200m/R500c.
