[tool] d-04 post_finding {"claim": "Benchmark comparison. The redshift trend of the thermal HSE mass is set by profile shape: the scaled T at R500 drops 12.4%, partly offset by a 3.7% s
[finding] f-014 Benchmark comparison. The redshift trend of the thermal HSE mass is set by profile shape: the scaled T at R500 drops 12.4%, partly offset by a 3.7% steepening o
**Finding:** Benchmark comparison. The redshift trend of the thermal HSE mass is set by profile shape: the scaled T at R500 drops 12.4%, partly offset by a 3.7% steepening of the slope sum. This matches the sign of FLAMINGO's quoted cluster trend, where hydrostatic masses decrease with redshift at fixed true mass. The Nelson f_nth correction changes the size of the trend only through the assumed R200m/R500c evolution, reducing it from -9.2% to -5.3%. Feedback cannot yet be ranked because d-06 is pending. On SPT, the emulator cools by 12% at R500 and 30% at 2.7 R500 between z=0 and 0.5, while SPT reports about 40% cooler scaled temperatures for 0.6<z<1.2 than for 0.3<z<0.6. The redshift bins do not overlap, so this is qualitative only. No X-COP T/T500 or scaled-density values were quoted, so no profile comparison with X-COP was made.
