**Finding:** The fiducial R500 numbers now trace to tool output (tc-...-94 to -97, all bins shown). I differenced ln y between the r/R500 = 0.866 and 1.155 bins, whose geometric midpoint is 1.000, with spacing dln r = 0.2878, and took t(R500) as the geometric mean of the two bins. At z=0: dln rho/dln r = -2.545, dln T/dln r = -0.583, t = 0.592 and M_HSE,500c/M500 = 0.925, so b_HSE = (M_HSE - M500)/M500 = -0.075. At z=0.4987: -2.738, -0.505, t = 0.518, M_HSE/M500 = 0.840 and b_HSE = -0.160. The mass assumes kT500 = G mu m_p M500/(2 R500), so the absolute values depend on the T500 convention.
