**Finding:** The -1.86 vs -1.98 conflict at about 0.5 R500 comes from different bin pairs. At z=0, the central difference about the 0.487 bin (bins 0.365 and 0.649, spacing 0.5756) gives dln rho/dln r = -1.863 and dln T/dln r = -0.271 (f-004). The one-sided pair 0.487-0.649 (midpoint 0.562 R500) gives -1.981 and -0.306 (f-008). The pair 0.365-0.487 (midpoint 0.422) gives -1.745. The central difference at 0.487 at z=0.4987 gives -1.872 and -0.345. With these, M_HSE(<0.487 R500)/M500 = 0.408 (z=0) and 0.382 (z=0.4987). Central differences at the 1.54 bin (1.155-2.054) give -2.929/-0.912 with t = 0.430 and M/M500 = 1.272 at z=0, and -3.097/-1.072 with t = 0.380 and M/M500 = 1.221 at z=0.4987.
