**Critic, wave 2** — continue: 6 findings stand up to the evidence, 2 questioned ('Redshift shift compared with kinetic-AGN spread. Approximation: dln n/dln r is held at the': The arithmetic checks out from the f-010 t values and the fiducial density slopes (for example AGN-min 0.893 to 0.815 gives -9.1%, AGN-max 0.935 to 0.883 gives -5.7%). Two problems remain. First, the density slope is held at the fiducial values even though the d02_agnmin and d02_agnmax CGD files exist and were never read, so the M_HSE part is not a measurement of the feedback response. Second, the conclusion compares the redshift shift (-9.2%) with the fixed-z offset between variants (4.6-8.1%). That mixes a change in absolute bias with a change in the differential trend. The relevant robustness number is the spread of the shift itself across variants, -5.6% to -9.0%. That spread says the sign of the trend is robust and its size carries roughly a +-2% feedback systematic. It does not support 'cannot be cleanly separated'.; 'Benchmark comparison. The redshift trend of the thermal HSE mass is set by profile shape: ': It says 'feedback cannot yet be ranked because d-06 is pending', but d-06 closed in this same wave with f-010 and f-011, so that statement is out of date. The FLAMINGO redshift-trend quote and the SPT ~40% quote are said to be 'in references.bib', but the quoted excerpt of tc-...-89 cuts off at the FLAMINGO author line and does not contain either quote. The d-04 block reason also says FLAMINGO values lack verbatim cite() quotes. The benchmark agreement is therefore not shown in the evidence.).

Issues: Every evidence excerpt for f-010, f-012, f-015, f-016 and f-017 stops at the 0.0866 R500 bin. The 0.365, 0.487, 0.649, 0.866, 1.155, 1.54 and 2.054 bins the claims rely on are never shown. The tool calls are full-file reads and the hand arithmetic is internally consistent, so I accept the findings. Future findings should quote the specific rows they use.; The Nelson correction takes c200c=4 and Omega_m=0.3 at both redshifts. Concentration at fixed mass falls with redshift, which changes R500c/R200c and therefore R200m/R500c. Since f-013 shows that the entire redshift dependence of the correction comes from this ratio, the -5.3% corrected shift depends strongly on the assumption. The emulator's own cosmology (omega_m=0.1375, presumably Omega_m h^2) was also not used.; The overcorrection (f_nth of 21-26% at R500 against X-COP's ~6%) partly reflects Nelson+14's mass-selected sample of massive clusters (M200m >= 6e14 Msun/h) and its random-gas-motion definition. Before calling the emulator 'overcorrected', check that comparison against an X-COP-calibrated f_nth (2112.07554 or 1805.00034)..
